  "findings": [
    "SG6 L1: all six fully retained cohorts, with4..11 initially queued vehicles, have first-cross endpoint age1 s; full-cohort clearance endpoint ages8..22 s.",
    "SG3 L4: all six fully retained cohorts, with7..15 initially queued vehicles, also have first-cross endpoint age1 s; full-cohort clearance endpoint ages15..28 s.",
    "The larger queue needs more vehicle departures. These data describe longer whole-cohort clearance; they do not establish that front reaction or saturation startup lost time grows proportionally with queue count or physical length.",
    "SG6 L1 rank8 probes at n8 and n11 both have startup-excess midpoint0 s with sample-resolution bounds[-2,2] s. SG3 L4 n9/n10/n14/n15 startup midpoints are3/1/1/0 s, respectively; no proportional relation is supported.",
    "Queue count and physical extent are different: baseline SG3 n9 tail distance59.677 m exceeds n10 distance55.997 m, reflecting observed spacing/composition variation. No vehicle-length-based queue occupancy is inferred.",
    "Selected SG6 at1350 is terminal-censored and cannot support tail-clearance or startup-delay inference."
  ],
  "definitions": {
    "front_reaction": "Delay from actual green onset to first sustained movement of the first queued vehicle. Not measured by this cached crossing-only evidence.",
    "queue_release_propagation": "Time at which each initially queued vehicle begins sustained movement versus initial rank and distance. Cannot be reconstructed from stopbar crossing times alone; continuous speed histories are required.",
    "startup_lost_time": "Excess time consumed by initial queued departures relative to subsequent saturated queued headways; the present descriptive rank8 expression is C4-G-4*((C8-C4)/4). It is separate from first-cross lag and whole-queue clearance.",
    "whole_initial_queue_clearance": "Green onset to stopbar passage of the last vehicle already in the retained initial standing cohort. Later arrivals are excluded; this is not time until the approach is empty.",
    "physical_extent": "Distance of last initial queued vehicle front position from head, plus separate first-to-last front-position span; vehicle body lengths are unavailable.",
    "sampling_bounds": "Elapsed-time bounds account only for one-second native green-onset and crossing intervals. They are not confidence intervals, identification bounds, calibration proof, or protection against unobserved subsecond changes."
  },
  "confounders_and_limits": [
    "Single seed and only six complete episodes per selected lane; observations are temporally related and are not randomized queue-length interventions.",
    "Baseline and selected use different phase timing and green start times; red duration, residual queues, arrival platoons and traffic histories differ.",
    "Keep lane and geometry fixed when comparing: SG6 link52 lane1 and SG3 link66 lane4 are separate lane series with different movements and downstream conditions.",
    "Vehicle type/length, stopped gaps, head distance and acceleration are not controlled; queue count does not uniquely determine physical extent.",
    "Native1 s sampling can hide reaction differences, tied events and subsecond lane changes; observed continuous lane identity is not perfect subsecond proof.",
    "Lane changes, incomplete ordered prefixes, green already active at900 and end1350 censoring remain excluded or explicitly flagged.",
    "Later headways can reflect downstream receiving constraints and turning behavior; four headways after rank4 do not prove stationary saturation.",
    "No regression, correlation-based causal claim, proportionality assumption, blanket delay, or capacity adjustment is made."
  ],
  "recommendation": {
    "queue_length_proportional_startup_delay_supported": false,
    "controller_parameter_change_supported": false,
    "current_action": "Keep queue clearance, movement-release propagation and startup lost time separate. Do not calibrate an added queue-proportional delay from these data.",
